<%# The intention's two knobs, shared by the create form and the edit page so there is one
    place that states the rules (decisions/one-primitive-composed.md).

    Exposure comes first because it gates the count: on the edge, DNS points at the box,
    so a second box cannot serve the same hostname and asking for one states something no
    deploy will deliver. Both are refused at validation, not merely discouraged here. %>
<div class="exposure-pick">
  <div class="radio-cards">
    <div class="radio-row">
      <label class="radio">
        <%= f.radio_button :exposure, "edge", checked: install.exposure_edge? %>
        <%= icon "earth", size: 20 %>
        <span class="radio-label">On the edge</span>
        <small class="radio-hint">DNS points at the box, which terminates its own TLS.
          One box.</small>
      </label>
      <label class="radio">
        <%= f.radio_button :exposure, "balanced", checked: install.exposure_balanced? %>
        <%= icon "boxes", size: 20 %>
        <span class="radio-label">Behind a balancer</span>
        <small class="radio-hint">The box is a backend; DNS points at the balancer in
          front of it. One box or many.</small>
      </label>
    </div>
  </div>

  <label class="field"><span>How many boxes
    <%= hint "The intention — how many boxes should serve this app. Placing each one is a separate recorded act; nothing is provisioned automatically." %></span>
    <%= f.number_field :count, value: install.count || 1, min: 1, max: 50 %>
    <small class="muted">Only above 1 when behind a balancer, and only for stateless
      apps — an app that declares a volume is single-placement, since replicas would each
      keep their own copy of that data.</small>
  </label>

  <%# Said plainly rather than implied: choosing "behind a balancer" states the topology,
      it does not build one. The console does not yet manage a balancer, so the operator's
      own (Cloudflare, a Caddy they run, a cloud LB) is what makes the count real. %>
  <p class="stub-note"><%= icon "clock", size: 14 %>
    <span><strong>The console doesn't manage the balancer yet.</strong> Marking an app
    balanced says DNS points somewhere other than the box, and unlocks a count above 1 —
    but pointing a balancer at those boxes is still yours to do. A managed balancer, with a
    routing table reconciled from the installs behind it, is not built.</span></p>
</div>
